    "coding agents",
    "benchmark",
    "agent skills"
  ],
  "isLiveDataset": false,
  "rai:dataLimitations": "Scores measure agreement with declared public-code reference derivations, not clinical correctness. 26 of 28 tasks use MIMIC-IV and two use eICU, so the evidence is not database- or hospital-general. Row-level agent outputs and tool outputs are withheld, so outputs cannot be re-evaluated from this package alone. The July Claude campaign mixes Claude Code CLI versions and routing profiles for some tasks; see the harness sensitivity table.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "Task selection is critical-care focused and inherits the populations, documentation practices, and coding conventions of MIMIC-IV and eICU. Control subsets were purposively selected from pilot results and are not representative of all tasks.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "Derived from de-identified credentialed PhysioNet data. The open package keeps no source data, task databases, reference outputs, row-level agent outputs, or tool outputs. Events whose tool output could not be isolated are withheld whole. In the agent text that is kept, credentials, shifted datetimes, patient ages, and identifier-led rows are removed, MIMIC and eICU identifiers are pseudonymized, and local paths and user names are removed. Agent messages can still describe in words what the agent observed.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Auditing and reproducing the M4Bench paper tables; inspecting agent behavior, failure modes, and isolation checks. Not for clinical decision-making or for estimating clinical outcomes.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "Supports transparent evaluation of AI agents for supervised clinical research workflows. Misreading reference agreement as clinical validity could encourage unsupervised use of agent-derived clinical variables.",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": false,
  "prov:wasDerivedFrom": [
    {
      "@type": "sc:Dataset",
      "name": "MIMIC-IV v3.1",
      "url": "https://physionet.org/content/mimiciv/3.1/"
